# StreamLux App & Web Conventions

## Sports matches
- When a user taps any **live, upcoming, or finished match**, always open the arena inside the app WebView player.
- Redirect URL: `https://streamlux.vercel.app/sports/arena/{fixtureId}`
- Navigate via the `live` player route with the URL URL-encoded — never open the system browser and never use the legacy `sports` player route for match cards.
- Do not change the web sports watch page auto-failover behavior unless explicitly requested.

## Downloads
- All movie/TV downloads must stay **inside the app** — never launch an external browser for download flows.
- Primary: Vyla direct CDN dialog (`VylaDownloadDialog`).
- Fallback when no links or on error: **VidVault** portal in `VidVaultWebViewOverlay` at `https://vidvault.ru/` with TMDB ID pre-filled.
- On failure: show a clear message, keep the title in the local Room library (`registerDownloadIntent`), and never crash or force-close the app.
- System `DownloadManager` for actual file saves is fine; the user must not be sent out to Chrome/browser to find downloads.

## Web (STREAMLUX)
- Downloads mirror native: **Option 1** = `VylaDownload` direct CDN links; **Option 2** = `VidVaultPortal` launcher → **new tab** at `https://vidvault.ru/` with TMDB pre-filled. Never iframe VidVault on web (iframe clicks redirect to ads).
- Option 2 must always be visible in the download dropdown, not only on failure.
- Register titles in Redux `downloadSlice` when download is requested.
- Streaming: VidKing default; include VidNest, TouStream, AnimeHub, Fsonic, Miruro, MeowTV fallbacks in `resolver.ts`.
- Sports web pages keep their own auto-failover — do not change unless explicitly requested.
